# Cray X-MP floating-point reference vectors.
#
# Source of the operands and expected results: the hard-coded test data of Andras Tantos's
# cray-sim, simulator/fp_test/fp_test.cpp (tables A, B, Sum, Product, Reciproc and the
# literal cases in main()). Only the numbers are taken, as facts; no code is copied.
#
# Format: OP A B RESULT FLAGS, all hexadecimal. OP is one of add sub mul mulh mulr mul2m
# recip. B is 0 for recip. FLAGS bit 0 is the floating-point range error.
#
# fp_test.cpp carries no flags. The FLAGS column here is what the Cray manuals prescribe
# (0 everywhere except the reciprocal of zero) and is not independent evidence.
#
# Not included, because cray-sim itself does not reproduce them:
#   mul 4005CAE20FC3F04D 3FFECB56F3138000 -> 4003A1262B15B48F   (live in main(); cray-sim and
#       this crate give ...B48E for 064; ...B48F is the X-MP 066 rounded product and also what
#       the reconstructed CRAY-1 staircase pyramid gives for 064)
#   add 000000000DEA1736 00000000399F9541 -> 000000004789AC77   (commented out; an integer sum)
#   mul 301C0BDB56AE0732 2213260D6B89030A -> 4001000000000000   (commented out)

